uld go  to King that three getting involved into  the game work to D one knowing that's  not gonna threaten this pawn right here  wants to start attacking some of the  other material Bishop to e3 defending  that material rook over here b1 but it's  all by himself there's just no way for  this rook to do anything King to g4 rook  to h1 attacking the pawn pawn h4 king g6  now the bishop centralizes with d3  and then pawn f5 King to f3 work over  here d1 just attacking the pawn but it's  still defendant can't really do too much  pawn F excuse me g4 and at this pot spot  Wesley so decides to go ahead and resign  wish you were to played a little bit  longer yes he is down as far as material  but not by much and yes he does need to  get his rooks playing a little bit  better together cuz right now they're  guro going around trying to attack and  you know white just has so much material  to defend against one so rook here but  it's not an easy endgame you could  definitely have your opponent make a  small mistake and you could find a draw  here Wesley so decides not so much today  and resigns hoping that he can come back  tomorrow but he does have his work cut  out for him any time a player knows that  all they have to do is go in and get a  draw to move on to the finals it's just  much easier for preparation many players  when they take a line in an opening they  try to keep themselves pretty open  because they don't know if their  opponents can make a mistake and they  want to have some chances to win if they  do if you know you're gonna draw you can  play specific lines that are very draw  and hard for your opponent's ever find  anything because you play these many  times over it and you know there's  there's no way for you to win but  there's also very limited ways for your  opponent to win so Shakir  congratulations to him on the victory  today it's gonna be going in tomorrow  looking for at least a draw and he will  be moving on to the finals in the other  game Alexa